<div class="ca-inner"><p class="ca-eyebrow">Your financial co-pilot</p><h2>Finance leadership that connects<br>the numbers to the next decision.</h2><p class="ca-intro">Centripetal provides embedded fractional CFO support for early-stage SaaS companies. We bring financial strategy and operating discipline together: the cash model, the capital plan, the board conversation, and the finance work that supports them.</p><div class="ca-split"><div><h3>Built for Seed through Series A</h3><p>Our focus is SaaS founders whose financial complexity has outgrown founder-owned spreadsheets and periodic bookkeeping. Companies with $2M+ in recurring revenue and/or $5M–$15M raised are a useful starting point for a conversation. The fit depends on your decisions, team, and operating needs.</p></div><div><h3>One connected finance function</h3><p>These areas of support work together within an agreed engagement. A fundraise draws on the same customer schedules, financial model, and reporting cadence your team needs to operate after the round.</p><a class="ca-link" href="guides/saas-finance-scorecard.html">Start with your finance foundation →</a></div></div><h2 style="margin-top:64px">The work we help you own.</h2><div class="ca-grid"><article class="ca-card"><p class="ca-eyebrow">Financial leadership</p><h3>Fractional CFO for SaaS</h3><p>An embedded financial co-pilot who connects your operating plan, cash position, and capital decisions.</p><a class="ca-link" href="services/fractional-cfo-for-saas.html">Explore fractional cfo for saas →</a></article><article class="ca-card"><p class="ca-eyebrow">Capital strategy</p><h3>Fundraising Readiness</h3><p>Prepare a financial model, diligence evidence, and use-of-proceeds plan that tell the same story.</p><a class="ca-link" href="services/fundraising-readiness.html">Explore fundraising readiness →</a></article><article class="ca-card"><p class="ca-eyebrow">Cash visibility</p><h3>Cash Flow & Runway Planning</h3><p>Connect collection timing, spending commitments, and hiring decisions to a maintained cash forecast.</p><a class="ca-link" href="services/cash-flow-runway-planning.html">Explore cash flow & runway planning →</a></article><article class="ca-card"><p class="ca-eyebrow">Investor communication</p><h3>Board & Investor Reporting</h3><p>Explain what changed, why it matters, and what decisions follow from the financial and operating data.</p><a class="ca-link" href="services/board-investor-reporting.html">Explore board & investor reporting →</a></article><article class="ca-card"><p class="ca-eyebrow">Financing decisions</p><h3>Venture Debt Readiness</h3><p>Evaluate financing fit, prepare lender information, and model repayment alongside the capital plan.</p><a class="ca-link" href="services/venture-debt-readiness.html">Explore venture debt readiness →</a></article><article class="ca-card"><p class="ca-eyebrow">Operating foundation</p><h3>Treasury & Finance Operations</h3><p>Make banking controls, close processes, and back-office responsibilities clear and dependable.</p><a class="ca-link" href="services/treasury-finance-operations.html">Explore treasury & finance operations →</a></article></div><div class="ca-split" style="margin-top:64px"><div><h3>How the engagement begins</h3><ol><li><strong>Understand the decisions.</strong> Start with your company, current finance ownership, and the decisions approaching.</li><li><strong>Assess the foundation.</strong> Review the financial model, reporting, cash processes, and responsibilities behind those decisions.</li><li><strong>Agree on the priorities.</strong> Establish the scope, owners, and working cadence; revisit them as the business changes.</li></ol></div><div><h3>What you should expect to use</h3><p>A maintained operating model, cash visibility, clear reporting, and a finance lead who can explain the assumptions. The exact deliverables follow your needs and the agreed scope.</p><a class="ca-link" href="guides/series-a-diligence-readiness.html">See the evidence investors ask for →</a></div></div><h2 style="margin-top:56px">Questions founders ask.</h2><details><summary>How does a fractional CFO work with our bookkeeper?</summary><p>Your bookkeeper records and reconciles transactions. Centripetal connects the books to forecasts, financing decisions, reporting, and finance operations, coordinating with your existing team and specialists.</p></details><details><summary>Is this only support for a fundraise?</summary><p>Fundraising is one inflection point. The same financial foundation supports ongoing hiring, spending, board reporting, treasury, and operating decisions. Engagement priorities can evolve with the company.</p></details><details><summary>What happens when we need an internal finance leader?</summary><p>The finance infrastructure should support that transition. Centripetal can help with the move to an internal VP Finance or finance leader, with documented processes and a clear handoff.</p></details><p class="ca-footer"><a class="ca-link" href="contact.html">Talk through the finance work in front of you →</a></p></div>